1988	 *
1989	 * The DISK_EXPAND handler advances `Server.extraDiskGB` only AFTER the disk has
1990	 * really grown, so that field is the ground truth for "did the customer get what
1991	 * they paid for". We refund only when it never reached the job's target — which
1992	 * also keeps this safe against the partial-success case (disk grown, filesystem
1993	 * left for the customer to grow by hand): that path completes successfully, sets
1994	 * extraDiskGB, and is therefore never refunded.
